//? Title: Self-Attention GAN: Spatial Mixing with Two Explicit Caches
//? Subtitle: Unscaled attention, zero residual gates and a complete weak MNIST experiment
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A compact spatial-patch GAN fits 1000 balanced MNIST images. Both generator and discriminator
use unscaled softmax attention across sixteen spatial tokens, with query/key width 2, value
width 4 and feature width 8. A scalar residual gate starts at zero. All twelve kernels use
cached spectral normalization: sixteen warm-up iterations precede fitting, then D's cache
advances before D and G's cache before a fresh G write. Two Adam states perform 96 writes
each over three fixed epochs. The complete editable native program preserves the original
checkpoint, derivatives, attention controls and weak grey samples. Small algebra and a
controlled three-token example explain nonlocal mixing; trained controls show that this
mechanism operates without establishing realistic generation or semantic localization.
)
\toc

> Follow pixels, spatial tokens and the two caches

The reference is [Zhang et al., Self-Attention Generative Adversarial Networks
(2018/2019)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08318). This repository's small teaching variant
uses dense shared patch maps rather than the paper's convolutional ImageNet architecture.
G maps Gaussian noise 16 through spectral dense 128/tanh to sixteen 8-feature tokens;
a spectral attention block mixes those tokens before a shared 8-to 49 sigmoid decoder
assembles sixteen 7×7 patches into 28×28 pixels. D extracts the same patches, embeds 49-to 8
with tanh, adds learned 16×8 positions, mixes tokens, averages positions and predicts one
raw source score. Both networks use attention and spectral normalization. No digit label
enters fitting; the architecture, seeds and short schedule follow the frozen source.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/self_attention_gan_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
