> The held-out samples remain weak

| Fixed final diagnostic | Value |
|---|---:|
| D objective |1.3446242809|
| G objective |0.8631716371|
| Coarse-pixel MMD² |0.1177780628|
| Repeated fitting-mean MMD² |0.0001357794|
| D real/fake source accuracy |0.000/1.000|
| Generated mean pixel |0.4984095126|
| Mean per-pixel variance across generated rows |0.0004166329|

Source accuracy uses raw score≥0 for real and score<0 for fake.
It measures this discriminator on these two sources, not digit recognition, calibration
or sample realism. The gallery retains the first 40 fixed-bank outputs, without choosing
attractive samples. Most remain grey fields rather than convincing digits. The real-source accuracy is zero even though every generated row is classified fake.
This weak game and grey gallery provide no evidence of a successful image model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/self_attention_gan_generated.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
