> Changed noise is a control, not evidence of realistic samples

Seed 4877 supplies the changed bank; the zero bank has the same shape. The restored G
responds to both changes, while standalone generation on the fixed bank matches the
full forward bit for bit. The first sample agrees between single and batch inference
(maximum error 0). Every saved weight and cache column restores exactly, and all diagnostic calls leave
all four stores unchanged. Responsiveness proves dependence on the input, not useful mode
coverage, diversity of recognizable digits or convergence.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/self_attention_gan_noise.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
