> Perturb one trained token and measure other output positions

The frozen control takes the first two held-out attention inputs for each network and
adds 1 to feature 0 of token 0. Existing weights and cache stay fixed. The plotted quantity
is max absolute output change over both rows and all 8 features at each of the 15 untouched
positions. It excludes the modified token's direct residual input change. The maximum
nonlocal changes are about.000728369 in G and.000387209 in D. Attention therefore mixes
spatial information in both fitted networks, but the effects are small and samples remain
weak. These controls establish dependence on other tokens rather than realistic images,
disentanglement or semantic attention localization.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/self_attention_gan_effect.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> c;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/self_attention_gan/attention_controls.npz"))
    c.emplace(k, v);
  std::vector<double> axis, g, d;
  for (int t = 1; t < 16; ++t) {
    axis.push_back(t + 1);
    for (int group = 0; group < 2; ++group) {
      auto   key    = std::to_string(group) + "/";
      double effect = 0;
      for (int b = 0; b < 2; ++b)
        for (int f = 0; f < 8; ++f)
          effect = std::max(
              effect,
              std::abs(
                  c.at(key + "output").at({b, t, f}) -
                  c.at(key + "modified_output").at({b, t, f})));
      (group ? d : g).push_back(effect);
    }
  }
  double maximum =
      std::max(*std::max_element(g.begin(), g.end()), *std::max_element(d.begin(), d.end()));
  std::print(
      "Maximum OTHER-token effect: G={} ; D={}. All checkpoint values unchanged.\n",
      *std::max_element(g.begin(), g.end()),
      *std::max_element(d.begin(), d.end()));
  for (auto& value : g)
    value *= 1e4;
  for (auto& value : d)
    value *= 1e4;
  maximum *= 1e4;
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.y_limits(0., maximum * 1.5)
      .lines(axis, g, "G nonlocal change", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .points(axis, g, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4.)
      .lines(axis, d, "D nonlocal change", {220, 38, 38}, 2.)
      .points(axis, d, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4.)
      .x_label("Untouched token, shown2..16; source token 0 was modified")
      .y_label("Max absolute output change, in units of 1e-4")
      .title("Changing one input token affects other positions")
      .save_svg("build/self_attention_gan_effect.svg");
}
```
