\alttext(Generator and discriminator nonlocal output changes at every untouched spatial position.)

> Verification and limits

Both unchanged-source delegation and this report match all ten frozen archives/1226475
values exactly in dtype, shape and value bytes, both source PNGs, both TSVs and every
non-timing metric. Twelve first-phase probe archives additionally match 97010 native values
across initialization, both cache advances, initial/advanced gradients and selected D/G
writes. Existing Plain attention at scale 1 matches the source's initial and final G/D
attention outputs and all token/projection derivatives bit for bit. The shared dense
refactor also retains all 364381 frozen Spectral GAN probe values exactly.

The independent NumPy checker imports no datamunge and performs no fitting. It checks
892521 forward values,15600 native derivatives,71 final scalar finite differences, all 355
cache values,16 warm-up iterations per network,3735 checkpoint values and 3000 fitting-row
visits. It reproduces patch permutations, unscaled softmax, stopped spectral-column
normalization derivatives, gamma-zero identity, trained attention and noise controls,
and state-D-state-fresh-G ownership. Native, Python and R component checks also cover
owned fields, malformed inputs, live continuous paths and explicit host-owned writes.
Component coverage does not complete independent Python/R full experiment loops.

This is one short fixed-seed run without an uncertainty analysis, seed sweep or paper-scale
image benchmark. Small nonlocal effects and normalized attention rows do not establish
semantic explanations. The gallery, poor real-source classification and much better
constant-mean MMD baseline remain visible; no convergence or generation-quality claim
follows from these mechanism and numerical checks.
